<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Cemig cut to neutral.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Cemig cut to neutral.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Oppenheimer &amp; Co said on Friday it had cut its rating for Braziian utility Companhia Energetica de Minas Gerais, or Cemig, to neutral from outperform.</p>
<p>-- The firm wrote in an analysis that it had downgraded the stock because it had surpassed a price target.</p>
<p>-- &quot;We continue to like Cemig and find any weaknesss a buying opportunity.&quot;</p>
<p>-- The company was trading down 1.50 to 47.50 in Sao Paulo on Friday.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
</text>
